    "explanation": "The disputed amount is the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee on trip TRP-02730 (EV-FARE-02730, total_charged 4.50; the same figure is platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd in EV-TRIP-02730). That fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full. No driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhy the fee fails. A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold. The driver did arrive: EV-GPS-02730 shows one continuous run of 9 qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 06:28:20 to 06:29:39 (79 seconds), and EV-TRIP-02730 carries the 'arrived' event at 06:28:20, so limbs (a) and (b) are met. Limb (c) is not. The free waiting period in force is 180 seconds (EV-TRIP-02730, platform_policy.free_wait_sec), and POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the arrival tap. The driver held position 79 seconds and cancelled at 06:29:42 — a 101-second shortfall. Limb (d) fails for the same reason: the termination did not fall at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed. POL-NS-06 therefore applies on its own terms (effective dwell shorter than the free waiting period) and refunds the cancellation fee in full, with no compensation.\n\nIndependently, POL-NS-04. The rider sent 'coming out now' at 06:29:20 (EV-CHAT-02730); the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call (EV-TRIP-02730, in_app_calls empty) before cancelling 22 seconds later; and the rider's track places her device 15.7–23.2 m from the pin on all 30 fixes, well inside the 100 m STANDARD radius. On those limbs the rider is exonerated with no driver compensation. Either route reaches the same result.\n\nWhat I did with the arguments. The driver's arrival and fare-integrity points are accepted: the arrival is genuine (EV-GPS-02730, dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), so POL-NS-05 does not fire and no false-arrival referral arises, and the 4.50 charge reconciles with platform_policy, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. The driver's concession that the marker is a BUTTON press (POL-NS-12) is accepted — the platform-confirmed-arrival shortcut is unavailable, and the arrival and dwell are read from the exported trace, which is what shows the 79-second dwell. The driver's compensation claim (POL-NS-07, SGD 3.60) is rejected: compensation arises only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-06 displaces it. The anti-farming figures (no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 65, a rate of about 0.015) are accepted but change nothing, since no compensation is payable. The rider's own phrasing that she 'cancelled after under two minutes' is not the record: the trip was terminated by the driver at 06:29:42, about 9.5 minutes after acceptance, and the refund rests on the driver's short dwell and POL-NS-04, not on that assertion. The driver's request to look at the rider's no-show history is not a ground of decision: POL-GEN-01 makes prior_no_show_flags and every profile field except the counters a clause names context only, and the citable trailing-window counter, no_show_disputes_30d, is 1 — below the POL-NS-09(d) threshold of 3. Reputation is not evidence about this trip.\n\nNo referral. No clause produces one here: RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises, so there is no mis-selected-code driver-education item; the arrival marker is genuine, so there is no POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival record; and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip, so no POL-NS-09 escalation packet issues.\n\nConfidence. Every artifact the ruling rests on — EV-GPS-02730, EV-TRIP-02730, EV-CHAT-02730 and EV-FARE-02730 — carries weight_multiplier 1.0, and none is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The missing advisory EV-ADVIS-02730-01 (weight 0.0) carries no fact the ruling needs and does not lower the cap. The amount, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes on issue."
