    "explanation": "The SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02730 is refunded in full to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhy the charge does not stand. To charge a no-show fee the driver had to hold position inside the pickup geofence for the free waiting period in force (POL-NS-01 limb (c)). The record's platform_policy puts that period at 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, and the fare ledger carries the same 180 s). On the driver's own telemetry (EV-GPS-02730) he held position in-geofence for a single continuous run of 79 seconds, from 06:28:20 to 06:29:39, and terminated the trip at 06:29:42 under RIDER_NO_SHOW — a shortfall of 101 seconds. POL-NS-06 therefore makes the fee not chargeable and refunds it in full, and POL-NS-01 limb (c) fails, so the fee cannot stand under the anchor clause either. The rider's suggestion that she 'cancelled after under two minutes' is not the record — the driver cancelled, about 9.5 minutes after acceptance — but the refund does not rest on her timing; it rests on the driver's short dwell.\n\nPOL-NS-06 limb (i). Both sides' accumulation arguments were discarded at Step 1: limb (i) needs a present and populated traffic advisory, and EV-ADVIS-02730-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0. Neither advocate disclosed that impairment and its issue code (MISSING_ARTIFACT) in the claim, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires, so the claims were discarded. I reach the same substantive conclusion anyway: there is a single in-geofence run, so there is no second interval to sum.\n\nThe arrival marker (POL-NS-05). At 06:28:20 the trace places the driver in-geofence at a dwell_start_offset of 0.0 s. He was not more than 300 m from the pin and not travelling at or above 15 km/h, so the 'I'm Here' marker is not false, POL-NS-05 does not fire, and no false-arrival referral arises under POL-NS-05(ii).\n\nDriver compensation (POL-NS-07). The driver is paid only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full or POL-NS-10(g) applies. POL-NS-01 fails at limb (c), and this was a driver-initiated termination, not a rider cancellation after the dwell had elapsed, so limb (g) does not apply either. The anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1, rate 0.015, both under the POL-NS-07 thresholds), but that is beside the point: with no chargeable fee there is nothing to pay 80 percent of. The claim for SGD 3.60 compensation (80 percent of SGD 4.50) is rejected.\n\nRider presence and contact (POL-NS-04). The rider's device sat 15.7–23.2 m from the pin across all 30 of her fixes, inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, and she messaged 'coming out now' at 06:29:20 — 22 seconds before the driver cancelled and cancelled without replying. Those facts independently support a full refund and are consistent with it; the outcome does not need them.\n\nCounter-statement and profiles (POL-GEN-01). The driver's statement invites the tribunal to weigh the rider's no-show history. prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter and is context only — it cannot carry an adverse finding about this trip. The citable trailing figure, no_show_disputes_30d, is 1, below the 3 that POL-NS-09(d) requires, so no escalation arises on that ground.\n\nNo escalation is triggered under POL-NS-09: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; the same-party repeat-dispute counts are both 0; the anti-farming check is clear; and the deciding artifact (EV-GPS-02730, weight 1.0) is COMPLETE, not impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d). The fare ledger reconciles with the net fee under POL-NS-08(d) (4.50 = 4.50), so there is no fare-integrity defect. No clause produces a referral on these facts.\n\nConfidence and execution. The deciding fact — the short in-geofence dwell — is carried by EV-GPS-02730 (weight 1.0) and corroborated by the trip record's own events; the cap is 1.0 and nothing is discounted, so confidence is stated at 0.90. The amount refunded is SGD 4.50, the cancellation-fee line charged on EV-FARE-02730 (total_charged 4.50, fee_charged 4.50, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). Driver compensation is null. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is at or below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so under POL-GEN-05 this ruling executes automatically."
